{"duration_api_ms":283817,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"24535a9f-7b34-4124-ab7f-db02f0dfbee6","total_cost_usd":0.32837799999999995,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12676,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":27767,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":20958},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12676,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":27767,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12676,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12676},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":27767,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12676,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.32837799999999995,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":20958,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"Only 1 of 20 evaluated designs is feasible (C-a041a8f492d8, q=407 kW/m2, T=447.7 K, HV 0.013). 9 designs failed on geometry. The failure messages fit a closed-form rule: with nose radius = bluntness*d, shoulder radius = 0.1*d and half-angle theta, the fore-cone length is positive only if (bluntness-0.1)*cos(theta) < 0.4. It reproduces the reported negative lengths (-2229, -54 and -51.5 mm) and does not depend on diameter. The margins imply limits of max_g <= 12 and T <= 450 K. Heat-shield mass fraction is roughly 0.088*d^2 (0.10-0.12*d^2 for low theta and low bluntness), so d must be below about 3.2-3.3 for blunt, high-theta shapes. Max g follows the flight-path angle almost alone: g ~ 6 + 95*sin(|gamma|), so g stays under 12 only for gamma shallower than about -3.6 deg. HV is (1-q/2.5e6)*(450-T)/150, so the largest gain comes from lowering bondline T. The heat-flux data fit q ~ K*sqrt(sin|gamma|/(d^2*Rn)) with K of 6-8.4e6. The temperature rise fits dT ~ 42.6*(q/sin|gamma|/1e6)^0.45. Large d and large Rn = b*d lower both objectives, so the promising region is d ~3.0-3.3, bluntness ~1.0-1.2, theta ~66-70 deg and gamma ~ -3 to -3.6 deg.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-a041a8f492d8: the only feasible design, d=2.65, b=0.636, theta=60, gamma=-1.59. T=447.7 K sits at the 450 K limit and margin_mass=0.358.\",\"C-cb5a1ab6b4d5: d=3.59, b=0.946, theta=63, gamma=-7.07 gives q=360 kW/m2 and T=369 K. Large Rn=3.4 m keeps q low even at steep entry, but g=18.6 and mass margin -0.145 make it infeasible. This shows the blunt, large-d shape has good thermal performance.\",\"C-180459c370c5 (d=3.1, gamma=-2.87): g=10.77, T=427 K, q=492 kW/m2, failing only on mass (-0.10). C-72d2b71ac4b2 (d=3.78) has mass margin -0.449, and mass margins in the 0.088-0.114*d^2 range put the mass limit near d~3.2-3.3.\",\"C-e30c1a5dba83 (gamma=-4.25, g=12.69), C-8090f66f0b58 (-4.97, 13.94) and C-0108a5ff122b (-5.33, 15.36) are g-limited. C-72d2b71ac4b2 (-2.55, g=10.51) and C-180459c370c5 (-2.87, g=10.77) are not, so gamma must be shallower than about -3.6 deg.\",\"C-d908ebc2f4b2 (b=0.868, theta=56.7), C-f5b5877d7e46 (b=0.788, theta=52) and C-813c08b0d84f (b=0.59, theta=23.2) are all invalid. Valid blunt designs such as C-0108a5ff122b (b=0.98, theta=68.8) and C-cb5a1ab6b4d5 (b=0.946, theta=63.4) sit below the (b-0.1)cos(theta)=0.4 boundary. High bluntness therefore needs high theta.\",\"C-cd84ccaadeb7: small d=1.37 at gamma=-2.06 gives T=493 K, infeasible. Small diameters (high ballistic coefficient) push both q and T up, so d should be large.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak heating scales roughly as sqrt(rho_peak/Rn)*V^3. A larger diameter lowers the ballistic coefficient and a larger nose radius lowers stagnation heating, so both cut q and the integrated heat load that drives bondline temperature. A steeper entry shortens the pulse and lowers T but raises peak q and g, so g<=12 caps steepness at about -3.6 deg. The mass fraction (area-driven) caps d at about 3.2-3.3. Bluntness (Rn=b*d) is limited by the geometry rule, so pushing it up requires theta near 66-70 deg. Together the best trade-offs should be d~3.2, b~1.05-1.2, theta~68-69.5, gamma from -1.6 to -3.6, giving q ~230-300 kW/m2 and T ~380-410 K. That is far above the current HV.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The q, T and g models are quick fits to 11 valid points, and the constants K and the dT exponent drift with gamma and shape. The mass limit near d=3.3-3.4 and the g limit near gamma=-3.6 are inferred, not observed. The blunt, high-theta corner (b>1.1, theta~69.5) has no valid data at all. Effects of theta and bluntness on Cd, mass and T are extrapolated. The geometry rule is fitted from failure messages and could have small errors near the boundary.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb5a1ab6b4d5\",\"rationale\":\"Anchor exploit design: large d just under the mass limit, blunt high-theta shape, gamma near the g limit for minimum T.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.05,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":287000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":385,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the central hypothesis that large Rn plus moderate gamma cuts both objectives; g≈11.8 is close to the limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb5a1ab6b4d5\",\"rationale\":\"Same shape as the anchor with shallower gamma=-3.0 to trace the front and keep g margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.05,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":390,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gives a safe feasible point with low q and T; g≈10.9 leaves comfortable margin.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb5a1ab6b4d5\",\"rationale\":\"Shallower gamma=-2.5 trades higher T for lower q on the same shape.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.05,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":256000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Spreads the front toward lower q and shows how T rises as gamma gets shallower.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb5a1ab6b4d5\",\"rationale\":\"Gamma=-2.0 explores the low-q end of the trade-off.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.05,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":248000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether shallow entry keeps T below 450 K with a large blunt body, and how q flattens.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a041a8f492d8\",\"rationale\":\"Very shallow gamma=-1.6 with a big blunt body extends the front to the minimum-q corner. The only feasible design already sits at this gamma.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.05,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":233000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extreme low-q corner of the front; also checks T stays under 450 K with a large d.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb5a1ab6b4d5\",\"rationale\":\"d=3.3 checks whether the mass fraction still passes near its predicted limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.05,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":266000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":385,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the mass-fraction boundary; predicted mass margin is only about 0.04.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb5a1ab6b4d5\",\"rationale\":\"d=3.0 is a diameter reduction with more mass margin (about 0.2) to see how much q and T degrade.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.05,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":306000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":390,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Diameter sensitivity at fixed shape and gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb5a1ab6b4d5\",\"rationale\":\"d=2.6 checks the diameter trend with a large mass margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.6,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.05,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":380000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the mid-front and validates the q ~ 1/d scaling.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb5a1ab6b4d5\",\"rationale\":\"Small d=2.2 tests how strongly q and T rise at lower diameter.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.05,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":487000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":412,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Bounds the diameter trend and checks that small blunt bodies remain thermally feasible.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb5a1ab6b4d5\",\"rationale\":\"Very blunt, big body at shallow gamma=-2.5 aims at low q (about 230 kW/m2).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":229000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":390,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the blunt corner of the geometry boundary ((b-0.1)cos(theta)=0.385) and its effect on q, T and mass.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb5a1ab6b4d5\",\"rationale\":\"d=3.4 with high bluntness is a deliberate boundary probe of the mass-fraction limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.4,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":237000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":381,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Predicted mass ratio is about 0.98-1.0, so the result pins down the d limit and shows whether high-theta blunt shapes lighten the shield.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb5a1ab6b4d5\",\"rationale\":\"d=3.2 with bluntness 1.2 at theta 69.5 and gamma=-3.5 is the highest-Rn exploit design.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":260000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":382,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Best predicted corner: Rn=3.84 m combined with a steep-but-legal gamma. Tests whether more bluntness lowers T further.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb5a1ab6b4d5\",\"rationale\":\"d=3.1, b=1.2, gamma=-3.0 is a lower-risk blunt design with mass and g margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":268000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":389,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds a safe-margin point in the blunt region to measure the bluntness effect against #2 and #12.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a041a8f492d8\",\"rationale\":\"Moderate bluntness 0.85 at theta=66 tests how much q and T are lost when Rn is reduced from the 1.05-1.2 designs.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.85,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":334000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Bluntness sensitivity at fixed d and gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a041a8f492d8\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness 0.6 at theta 68 is closer to the current feasible design and shows the cost of low Rn.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.6,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":425000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Completes a bluntness sweep at d=3.1 and covers the mid-q region of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a041a8f492d8\",\"rationale\":\"Mid cone angle 52 deg with b=0.7 checks theta sensitivity of mass and heating while staying inside the geometry boundary (0.369).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.7,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":52.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":386000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Isolates theta's effect (area, Cd, mass fraction) and gives the model information on lower-theta shapes.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-180459c370c5\",\"rationale\":\"Low-theta, low-bluntness shape (theta 40, b 0.5) with d=2.8 reduced from the mass-infeasible C-180459c370c5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.8,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.5,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":40.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":507000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether the low-theta family can be made feasible, and shows how much mass fraction depends on theta at d~2.8.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb5a1ab6b4d5\",\"rationale\":\"Same as the anchor with gamma=-3.6, right at the predicted g limit (g≈11.97), to locate the steepest legal entry.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.05,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":288000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":384,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Pins down the g boundary; a pass means steeper gamma is usable for lower T later.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb5a1ab6b4d5\",\"rationale\":\"A small step from C-cb5a1ab6b4d5 (b 0.95, theta 64) to d=3.2 and gamma=-3.4 tests whether the earlier thermal excellence carries over once mass and g are legal.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.95,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":64.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":297000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":388,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A near-copy of a shape known to be valid and thermally strong, moved into the feasible d and gamma window.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb5a1ab6b4d5\",\"rationale\":\"d=3.0, b=1.2, gamma=-3.6 combines a good mass margin, high Rn and a steep entry.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":291000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":385,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether a smaller d with high bluntness keeps the low q and T of the larger designs while leaving mass margin about 0.2.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":226457,"type":"result","duration_ms":283905,"uuid":"b6d6f30f-d13f-4c94-9e4b-b298d6043ec8","ttft_stream_ms":1447,"time_to_request_ms":87,"first_content_frame_ms":1447,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
